    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d632">

                <pb facs="0501" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-13T17:00:00+08:00">December 13, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 13—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Dr. Taylor of Anking telephoned again at 4:15, transmitted statement from
                    Atcheson that survivors were in danger at Hohsien. Dr. Taylor stated that he
                    thought danger was due to fighting there. Atcheson stated that Gassie<anchor
                        n="62" xml:id="d632-f1"/> had a wound in the leg. I, in fear<anchor n="63"
                        xml:id="d632-f2"/> of members Embassy staff unhurt. Department please inform
                    Mrs. Paxton.<anchor n="64" xml:id="d632-f3"/> British gunboat reported at 3
                    o’clock this afternoon that it had been off Hohsien for over half hour and could
                    see no signs of life on north bank; that Standard Oil Company’s <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Meian</hi> was beached and deserted, apparently hit by
                    bombs on bridge; that <hi rendition="#italic">Panay’s</hi> outboard sampan had
                    been recovered from mud half a mile below <hi rendition="#italic">Meian;</hi>
                    that Socony ship <hi rendition="#italic">Meihsia</hi> was burning fiercely at
                    Kaiyuan wharf on right bank of river and that <hi rendition="#italic">Bee</hi>
                    was proceeding to investigate.</p>
                <p>Repeated Shanghai and Peiping. Peiping please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d632-f1" n="62" xml:id="d632-f1-content">
                <p>Emile P. Gassie, clerk of the Embassy in China.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d632-f2" n="63" xml:id="d632-f2-content">
                <p>Sentence apparently garbled at this point.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d632-f3" n="64" xml:id="d632-f3-content">
                <p>John Hall Paxton, Second Secretary of Embassy in China, received a knee
                    injury.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
